Mapping Personal Data Inventory for GDPR Compliance
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Build a simple Record of Processing Activities (RoPA) using a CSV-based data inventory
Identify data sources, data subject categories, and processing purposes
Tag sensitive/special category data (biometric, health)
Document lawful basis and retention periods per GDPR Article 30 and GCC PDPL
Export a RoPA report for review by a Data Protection Officer (DPO)
Prerequisites
Basic familiarity with the Linux terminal (navigating folders, editing files)
No prior privacy/legal knowledge required — key terms are explained below
A single Linux machine (provided via Start Lab)
Key terms:

RoPA: Record of Processing Activities — a log of how personal data is used
Data Subject: The person the data belongs to (e.g., customer, employee)
Lawful Basis: The legal reason for processing data under GDPR (e.g., consent, contract)
Special Category Data: Sensitive data like health, biometric, or religious data
